We construct the point  $F$  on  $AD$  such that  $BF\perp AD$ , so we have the two pairs of similar triangles
\[\triangle ABF\sim\triangle ACE~~~~~\text{and}~~~~~\triangle DBF\sim \triangle DCE.\]

This gives the ratios
\[\dfrac{AF}{AE}=\dfrac{AB}{AC}=\dfrac{1}{k}~~~~~\text{and}~~~~~\dfrac{DF}{DE}=\dfrac{DB}{DC}=\dfrac{1}{k},\]
(which implies that  $(A,D;E,F)=-1$ , as a note) and so we can write  $AF=x,AE=xk,DF=y$  and  $DE=yk$  for some  $x$  and  $y$  such that  $AF+FD+DE=AE$ , i.e.
\[x+y+yk=xk\Longrightarrow 1+\dfrac{y}{x}+\dfrac{y}{x}k=k\Longrightarrow \dfrac{y}{x}=\dfrac{k-1}{k+1}.\]

From here, our desired ratio is hence
\[\dfrac{AD}{AE}=\dfrac{x+y}{xk}=\dfrac{1}{k}+\dfrac{y}{xk}=\dfrac{1}{k}\left(1+\dfrac{k-1}{k+1}\right)=\dfrac{2}{k+1}.\]

