Write  $P(x) = (x + a)(x + b)$  with  $a,b > 1$  and  $|a - b| < 2$ . We are asked to prove that  $P(P(x)) = ((x + a)(x + b) + a)((x + a)(x + b) + b)$  is positive for all real  $x$ . It suffices to prove that  $(x + a)(x + b) + \min(a,b) > 0$  for any  $x \in \mathbb{R}$ . WLOG  $a > b$ .
\begin{align*}
(x + a)(x + b) + b &= \left( x + \frac{a + b}{2} \right)^2 - \frac{(a -  b)^2}{4} + b 
&\ge b - \frac{(a - b)^2}{4} 
&> b - 1 
&> 0
\end{align*}

