Let the incircle meet  $CD$  at  $R$  and  $AB$  at  $P$ . Let  $H$  point where  $AB$  is tangent to  $(DXF)$ .
Some angle chasing yields
\begin{align*}
\measuredangle CDF=\measuredangle DXF=\measuredangle EXF=\measuredangle EFA=\measuredangle BEF=\measuredangle CEF,
\end{align*} thus  $DFEC$  is an isosceles triangle. Hence,  $CR=CE=DF=DR$ , which means that  $R$  is the midpoint of  $CD$ .

Note that  $DF=DR=PH=AP+AH=AF+\sqrt{AF\cdot (AF+DF)}$ , which simplifies to  $DF=3AF$ , hence  $AH=2AP$ .
Now, we have easy finish by the coaxiality lemma,  $$ \frac{P(A,(DXF))}{P(A,(ERFP)))}=\frac{AH^2}{AP^2}=4=\frac{CD^2}{CR^2}=\frac{P(C,(DXF))}{P(C,(ERFP)))}, $$  we are done.

