Answer is  $\boxed{8}$ , achieved by taking  $a=c=x, b=d=y$  for any  $x,y$  satisfying  $4xy = x^2 + y^2$ . Now we show the value is at least  $8$ . Note that problem is cyclic wrt  $a,b,c,d$ . Now at least one of  $(a-c)(b-d),(b-d)(c-a)$  is  $\ge 0$ . WLOG  $(a-c)(b-d) \ge 0$  (as otherwise we can look at  $b,c,d,a$  instead of  $a,b,c,d$ ). Then, 
\begin{align*}
\frac{a}{b} + \frac{b}{c} + \frac{c}{d} + \frac{d}{a} &= \frac{ac + b^2}{bc} + \frac{ac+d^2}{da} = \frac{(a+c)(b+d) + b^2 - bd}{bc} + \frac{(a+c)(b+d) + d^2 - bd}{da} 
&= \left( \frac{a}{c} + 1 \right) \left( 1 + \frac{d}{b} \right) + \frac{b}{c} - \frac{d}{c} + \left(1 + \frac{c}{a} \right) \left( \frac{b}{d} + 1 \right) + \frac{d}{a} - \frac{b}{a} 
&= \left( \frac{a}{c} + 1 \right) \left( 1 + \frac{d}{b} \right) + \left(1 + \frac{c}{a} \right) \left( \frac{b}{d} + 1 \right) + \underbrace{(b-d) \left( \frac{1}{c} - \frac{1}{a} \right)}_{\ge 0}
\end{align*}
Now we are done by <details><summary>AM-GM</summary>$$ \left( \frac{a}{c} + 1 \right) \left( 1 + \frac{d}{b} \right) + \left(1 + \frac{c}{a} \right) \left( \frac{b}{d} + 1 \right) \ge \left( 2 \sqrt{\frac{a}{c}} \right) \left( 2 \sqrt{\frac{d}{b}} \right) + \left( 2 \sqrt{\frac{c}{a}} \right) \left( 2 \sqrt{\frac{b}{d}} \right) = 4 \left( \sqrt{\frac{ad}{bc}} + \sqrt{\frac{bc}{ad}} \right) \ge 4 \cdot 2 = 8 $$</details>.  $\blacksquare$

