Now by the law of sines, we have   $$ \frac{KA}{KT}=\frac{\sin\angle KTA}{\sin\angle KAT}=\frac{\sin\angle BTP}{\sin\angle PBT}=\frac{PB}{PT}=\frac{PA}{PT}=\frac{AP'}{PT} $$  Thus by SAS we have  $\triangle P'AK\sim\triangle PTK\sim\triangle BTA$ , implying  $\angle PBT=\angle TAB=\angle P'KA$ \end{document}</details>

