By the cosine law on  $\triangle ADO$  and  $\triangle OPC$ , we obtain that  $AO^{2}=DO^{2}+AD^{2}$  and  $OC^{2}=OP^{2}+PC^{2}-2\cdot OP\cdot PC\cdot \cos{\angle OPC}$ , hence we need
\begin{align*}
AD^{2}&=PC^{2}-2\cdot OP\cdot PC\cdot \cos{\angle OPC}
