\[ (d_1,d_2,d_3,d_4,d_1+d_2,d_1+d_2+d_3,d_1+\ldots+d_4) = (B_{1,2,4,6,3,5,7}) \]
and  $2k-1$  terms come up, at best. Now, seeing that whether or not  $B_7$  is exactly  $B_6+B_5$  doesn't matter, I switched  $B_6$  to  $B_5$  and this happens:
