[/asy]
By Step 2,  $P(2z-x)$  must lie below  $\overline{P(x)P(z)}$ , so the green line has a slope greater than the red line, which has a slope greater than the blue line. However, this means that  $P(y)$  lies more above  $\overline{P(x)P(2z-x)}$  than  $P(z)$ , contradicting the problem condition.</details>

<details><summary>Step 4</summary>[asy]
