The answer is  $\boxed{3}$ . Consider the following walk on the graph depicted below:
\begin{align*}
A_1 &\to A_2 \to B_2 \to C_2 \to C_1 \to D_1  &\to C_1 \to B_1 \to B_2 \to A_2 \to D_2  &\to C_2 \to B_2 \to B_1 \to A_1,
\end{align*}
during which the junction  $B_2$  is visited three times. 
