Furthermore,  $\sqrt {xyz} = \left (\dfrac {1} {x} + \dfrac {1} {y} + \dfrac {1} {z}\right) \sqrt {xyz} = \sqrt {\dfrac {xy} {z}} + \sqrt {\dfrac {xz} {y}} + \sqrt {\dfrac {yz} {x}}$ , so it suffices to show
\begin{align*}
\sum \sqrt {\dfrac {yz} {x} + x + y + z} \ge \sum \sqrt {\dfrac {xy} {z}} + \sum \sqrt {x}
\end{align*}
From AM-GM, 
