Consider the equation  $3y^4 + 4cy^3 + 2xy + 48 = 0$ , where  $c$  is an integer parameter. Determine all values of  $c$  for which the number of integral solutions  $(x,y)$  satisfying the conditions (i) and (ii) is maximal:
(i)  $|x|$  is a square of an integer;
(ii)  $y$  is a squarefree number.

Determine all real solutions  $(a_1,...,a_n)$  of the following system of equations:  $$ \begin{cases}a_3 = a_2 + a_1
a_4 = a_3 + a_2
...
a_n = a_{n-1} + a_{n-2}
a_1= a_n +a_{n-1} 
a_2 = a_1 + a_n \end{cases} $$

solution_md:
The solid  $P_t$  consists of
1. The parallelepiped  $P$  with volume  $V_P$ ;
2. Pieces of right prisms constructed on the faces of  $P$  with heights  $h$  that supply  $S_Pt$  total volume;
3. Pieces of cylinders leaning to the edges of  $P$ . Note that the four pieces of cylinders corresponding to some four parallel edges of  $P$  form a whole cylinder. Summing up the volume of this cylinder with the volumes of the other two cylinders corresponding to the other two quartets of parallel edges we get  $\frac{\pi}{4}L_Pt^2$  total volume;
4. Pieces of balls centered at the vertices of  $P$ . Again note that the eight pieces of the balls together form a complete ball of radius  $t$  whence the volumes of the ball pieces sum up to  $\frac{4}{3}\pi t^3$ .
Adding the calculated volumes we get  $$ V(P_t)=V_P+S_Pt+\frac{\pi}{4}L_Pt^2+\frac{4}{3}\pi t^3 $$  as wanted.

